    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\n`gx` open current filepath by `<cfile>` and `isfname`, which take slash into account, \nso `expand(\"<cfile>\")` of mini.files entry will get a slash prefixed path, which is not a real path.\n\nI know slash is used to make mini.files entry concealed.\n\nso make `isfname` not take slash into account will fix this, but seems not ok, because isfname is a global option, which will cause path contained slash not be opend.\n\nMaybe delete slash from `isfname` at event `MiniFilesExplorerOpen`  and set it back in event `MiniFilesExplorerClose` is a way to make gx works or use other char to make entry concealed. \n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. `lua MiniFiles.open()` \n2. `echo expand(\"<cfile>\")` \n3. see the result from 2 which is a wrong path",
