            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes, the default `gx` won't work inside 'mini.files' windows because it doesn't show the full path. The suggested solution is to [make custom buffer-local mappings](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/48f48e4b3f317e9da34ee7a01958b4c5018e2d34/doc/mini-files.txt#L522-L533) (the example uses `gX` instead of `gx` to work with default 'mini.operators' setup; change it to `gx` or some other key).",
